[Step 160] Q: The average age of 8 men increases by 2 years when two women are included in place of two men of ages 20 and 10 years. What is the average age of the women?
Ground truth: 23
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

Let the total age of the 8 men be M.

The average age of the 8 men is M/8.

When two women are included in place of two men of ages 20 and 10 years, the total age of the group becomes (M - 20 - 10) + (Age of first woman + Age of second woman).

We know the average age has increased by 2 years, so the new average age is (M/8 - 20 + Age of first woman + Age of second woman)/10.

