<start_working_out>
To solve this problem, we can start from the innermost function and work our way out.

We are given that $p(q(4)) = 7$. 

First, we calculate $q(4)$.
$q(4) = 3 \cdot 4 - b$
$q(4) = 12 - b$

Now, substitute the expression for $q(4)$ into $p(q(4))$.
$p(q(4)) = p(12-b)$
$p(12-b) = 2(12 - b) - 7$

Expand the expression for $p(12-b)$.
$p(12-b) = 24 - 2b - 7$
$p(12-b) = 17 - 2b$

